        "original_id": "d94131b3-cf80-5446-a83b-8752654f7629",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michaël Llodra, Juan Martín del Potro\n- Sports: men's tennis\n- Organizations: Association of Tennis Professionals\n- Achievements: Grand Slam championships, Olympic silver medal, singles titles, rankings\n\nFacts:\n- Juan Martín del Potro was born on 23 September 1988 and is an Argentinian professional tennis player.\n- Michaël Llodra is a successful doubles player with three Grand Slam championships and an Olympic silver medal.\n- Michaël Llodra has also succeeded in singles by winning five career titles.\n- Michaël Llodra has recorded singles victories over Novak Djokovic, Juan Martín del Potro, Tomáš Berdych, Robin Söderling, Jo-Wilfried Tsonga, Nikolay Davydenko, Janko Tipsarević, and John Isner.\n- Juan Martín del Potro was ranked world No. 24 in men's singles by the Association of Tennis Professionals.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
